# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF, regardless of which OS/editor touched a
# file (Visual Studio on Windows vs. other tooling). Git still checks files out using each
# contributor's own core.autocrlf setting - this only fixes what's stored in the repo, so
# `git status`/`git diff` stop being swamped by CRLF-vs-LF noise across the two environments
# that edit this codebase.
* text=auto

*.cs text
*.cshtml text
*.js text
*.css text
*.sql text
*.config text
*.csproj text
*.sln text
*.json text
*.md text
*.xml text
*.txt text
*.svg text

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
